<title>USA: Penwest files for hypertension drug.</title>
<headline>Penwest files for hypertension drug.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Wash. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Penwest Ltd said Wednesday a paragraph IV Abbreviated New Drug Application has been filed with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for controlled release nifedipine tablets incorporating Penwest's TIMERx oral controlled release technology.</p>
<p>The filing was made by Penwest's collaborative partner, Mylan Laboratories Inc, and is for the first generic alternative to Procardia XL, a calcium channel blocker for treating hypertension with a U.S. market of about $950 million in 1996, the company said.</p>
</text>
